---
// Privacy policy for the source-only site. It covers myne.md, not a server
// run by someone else; the app's sync and AI providers are chosen by the user.
// The German version is `datenschutz.astro`; change both in the same commit.
import LandingLayout from "../layouts/LandingLayout.astro";
import GlassNav from "../components/GlassNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { absoluteOg } from "../lib/og";

const title = "Privacy Policy — Myne";
const description =
  "What myne.md processes, what it does not, and how the source-only project handles hosting logs, email and self-hosted servers.";
const canonical = new URL("/privacy/", Astro.site!).toString();
const ogImage = absoluteOg("privacy", Astro.site!);
const effective = "25 November 2026";

const eyebrow = "font-size:11px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:14px;";
const h2 =
  "font-size:clamp(19px,2.2vw,25px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.02em;line-height:1.15;margin-top:56px;";
const body =
  "margin-top:14px;max-width:68ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink-3);";
const cardStyle =
  "border:1px solid rgb(var(--line-rgb) / 0.1);border-radius:12px;padding:22px;background:var(--paper-2);margin-top:22px;";
const listStyle = body + "padding-left:20px;";
---

<LandingLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogImage={ogImage}>
  <div style="font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink-1);background:var(--paper);min-height:100vh;">
    <GlassNav active="legal" />

    <section id="top" style="padding:var(--page-top) var(--gutter) 70px;">
      <div style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;">
        <div class="mono up" style={eyebrow}>Legal</div>
        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,50px);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p style={body}>
          Effective {effective}. This policy covers <strong>myne.md</strong> and the project's public
          infrastructure. It does not cover a sync server run by you or by someone else: that operator
          decides what it stores and is the controller for it. Myne runs no hosted sync, storage or
          account service of its own.
        </p>

        <div style={cardStyle}>
          <div class="mono up" style={eyebrow}>The short version</div>
          <p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink-3);">
            This is a static website. There are no accounts, no newsletter, no cookies, no analytics
            and no advertising. The only personal data the site processes is what your browser sends
            to fetch a page, what you put in an email to us, and a short-lived local firewall buffer
            that blocks brute-force requests. Your notes never reach this website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 style={h2}>Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          The site is hosted by <strong>Hetzner Online GmbH</strong>, Industriestr. 25, 91710
          Gunzenhausen, Germany, in its Falkenstein data centre. Hetzner processes request data on our
          behalf under an Art. 28 GDPR processing agreement. No data is transferred outside the EU.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          The web server keeps short-lived operational logs. Client IP addresses, ports and forwarding
          headers are filtered out of access and error logs; what remains is the host, requested path,
          status, timing and error trace needed to run and secure the site. A separate local fail2ban
          buffer keeps the client address for at most one hour (and at most about 2 MiB on disk) so
          that repeated abusive requests can be blocked. It is a security measure, not an analytics
          record, and it is deleted on that schedule.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          The legal basis is our legitimate interest in providing a secure website (Art. 6(1)(f)
          GDPR). We do not merge these logs with other data or use them to identify visitors.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          We set no cookies and run no analytics, tracking pixels or third-party scripts. If you switch
          the site to light mode, that choice is stored in your browser's local storage under the key
          <code>myne-theme</code>. It stays on your device, is written only when you click the switch,
          and is never sent to us. Clearing site data removes it.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Email</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          If you write to <a href="mailto:hello@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">hello@myne.md</a>,
          <a href="mailto:privacy@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">privacy@myne.md</a>,
          <a href="mailto:security@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">security@myne.md</a> or
          <a href="mailto:source@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">source@myne.md</a>, we receive
          your address, the message and anything you attach. We use it only to answer you or to handle
          the request (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR) and keep it only as long as needed for that purpose,
          a legal obligation, or the security of the project. We do not use it for marketing and do
          not sell it.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>The app and self-hosted servers</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          The Myne app is local-first: your vault is created and encrypted on your device. This policy
          does not describe what a self-hosted server, a sync provider or an AI provider does with the
          data you choose to send it; that is the operator's or provider's policy. If you enable sync,
          the server you configure holds ciphertext and the account metadata described in the app's
          documentation; you or your operator are the controller for that server.
        </p>
        <p style={body}>
          The app contains no telemetry and no analytics. Its update check and model downloads, when
          enabled, contact Myne's own origin with the version/platform or the requested file; the
          origin is configured not to keep client IP logs or analytics. No note content is sent.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Your rights</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict and port your personal
          data, and to object to processing based on legitimate interests. Write to
          <a href="mailto:privacy@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">privacy@myne.md</a>. Because the
          site has no accounts, most requests will concern an email you sent us or a server log; we
          will explain what we hold and what we cannot retrieve. You may also complain to a supervisory
          authority. Ours is the
          <span style="color:var(--ink-1);">Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und für das Recht auf
          Akteneinsicht Brandenburg</span>, Stahnsdorfer Damm 77, 14532 Kleinmachnow.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Who is responsible</h2>
        <div style={cardStyle}>
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink-3);">
            <strong>Myne contributors</strong><br />
            Potsdam, Germany<br />
            <a href="mailto:privacy@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">privacy@myne.md</a>
          </p>
          <p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink-3);">
            A postal address is being added with the Impressum. Until then,
            <a href="mailto:privacy@myne.md" style="color:var(--accent);">privacy@myne.md</a> reaches the
            controller. There is no data protection officer: the thresholds of § 38 BDSG are not met.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3 style="font-size:16px;font-weight:650;margin-top:32px;color:var(--ink-1);">Processors</h3>
        <p style={body}>
          Hetzner Online GmbH hosts the site and processes request data under an Art. 28 agreement.
          There is no CDN, analytics vendor, crash-reporting service or email delivery service in the
          site's path. The project's GitHub organisation is hosted by GitHub, Inc.; your use of GitHub
          is governed by GitHub's own privacy statement.
        </p>

        <h2 style={h2}>Changes</h2>
        <p style={body}>
          We may update this policy when the site or its infrastructure changes. The effective date
          above changes with it, and the previous text remains in the public repository history.
        </p>

        <p style={body + "margin-top:44px;font-size:14px;"}>
          Deutsche Fassung: <a href="/datenschutz/" style="color:var(--accent);">Datenschutzerklärung</a>.
          Terms: <a href="/terms/" style="color:var(--accent);">Terms</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</LandingLayout>
